  "selection_method": "Stratified, not random, and reproducible from this description. Population: all 100 rows in production model_signals (the entire customer-facing board — there is no larger pool to sample from). Two deliberate strata plus a curated hard-case overlay drawn FROM those strata (not additional rows):\n\n1. VERDICT-ELIGIBLE (comparable_n >= 8, engine.listing_identity.MIN_VERDICT_COMPARABLES): 30 of 43 available rows, one per brand where possible, deepest-n rows preferred for brand coverage.\n2. BOARD-ADMITTED BUT NOT VERDICT-ELIGIBLE (comparable_n 3-7, admitted at engine.listing_identity.MIN_COMPARABLES=3 but denied a buy_below): 30 of 57 available rows, same brand-coverage rule.\n3. KNOWN-HARD (16 of the 60, drawn from strata 1-2 above) — picked for named, code-grounded reasons, each stated verbatim on that row's hard_case_reason field: (a) three Off-White rows (605, 679, 690) — replica/authenticity risk, since engine/authenticity.py exists but DATA.md documents it is not wired into refresh_model_signals; (b) two rows at the HIGHEST price_iqr_eur on the board despite passing admission — Gucci Horsebit (625, IQR 588.0, n=20) and Balenciaga Hourglass (643, IQR 500.0, n=5) — wide dispersion at depth is the signature of mixed/contaminated comps; (c) two deep-n same-brand controls contrasting the tiny-n hard cases — Off-White Arrows (605, n=25) and Balenciaga Triple S (609, n=30); (d) a same-brand verdict-boundary PAIR one comp apart — Gucci GG Marmont (623, n=8, eligible) / Gucci Bamboo (655, n=7, denied) — plus a second boundary-adjacent row, Balenciaga Le Cagole (634, n=7); (e) Gucci Dionysus (658, n=4, IQR 209.75) for the same replica-risk reason at low n; (f) all four Jordan rows (641, 659, 689, 696) — engine/listing_identity.py's own comment warns family_of() must not walk 'Jordan 4' onto 'Jordan 1', and the _VARIANT_TAIL regex (low/mid/high/sb/og/tn/xl/vtg) exists specifically for names like 'Jordan 1 Low'; (g) the two lowest-non-Off-White data_quality_score rows, both with a NULL price_iqr_eur — Carhartt Double Knee (693, dq=38) and Adidas Forum Low (680, dq=46), an untested null-handling path.\n\nAll 19 brands present in model_signals are represented at least once. Exact result: 30 rows in the n>=8 stratum, 30 rows in the n=3-7 stratum, 16 of the 60 additionally flagged known-hard (hard_case_reason not null); the remaining 44 were selected by the plain brand-coverage/fill rule with no individual reason recorded — that distinction is preserved on purpose, not blurred.",
